.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- rsync with colon-path local names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I SRC
\&...
.I DEST
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR rsync (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation handles local colon-path
arguments.
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B rsync
from
.B PATH
(including remote
.I host:path
and
.I host::module
forms).
.PP
Colon-path rewriting applies to local
.B BASE:LEAF
arguments.
.I host:path
and
.I host::module
forms are not treated as colon-paths.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten command without executing it.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-archive
Archive mode (preserves most attributes).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-compress
Compress file data during transfer.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-links
Copy symlinks as symlinks.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-perms
Preserve permissions.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-times
Preserve modification times.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group
Preserve group.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-owner
Preserve owner (super-user only).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-devices
Preserve device files (super-user only).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hard\-links
Preserve hard links.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-acls
Preserve ACLs.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-xattrs
Preserve extended attributes.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-rsh=COMMAND
Specify remote shell (or
.BR \-\-rsh=COMMAND ).
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete extraneous files from destination.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude=PATTERN
Exclude files matching
.IR PATTERN .
.TP
.B \-\-include=PATTERN
Include files matching
.IR PATTERN .
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show progress during transfer.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Perform a trial run with no changes made.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation (local only;
remote paths require external rsync).
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-rsync\fR → \fBrsync\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR colon-scp (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
